  id: Extensor_carpi_radialis_muscle.R
  partName: Extensor_carpi_radialis_muscle.R
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle is responsible for extending the wrist joint and plays a crucial
    role in stabilizing it during movement. It ensures proper positioning of the
    limb, especially during weight-bearing activities. By maintaining wrist extension,
    it supports efficient locomotion and prevents collapse of the joint. '
  - The muscle works in coordination with other extensors to provide smooth and controlled
    motion. It is particularly important for maintaining balance and proper posture
    during walking, running, and standing.
